"level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key word “MUST” in this document is to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"id":"fnref1","href":"#fn1"}]}," when, and only when, it appears in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term “network upgrade” in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"id":"fnref2","href":"#fn2"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The character § is used when referring to sections of the Zcash Protocol Specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3","href":"#fn3"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms “Mainnet” and “Testnet” are to be interpreted as described in § 3.12 ‘Mainnet and Testnet’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4","href":"#fn4"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The symbol “",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mspace","children":[],"attrs":{"width":"0.1667em"}},{"tag":"mo","children":["⋅"]},{"tag":"mspace","children":[],"attrs":{"width":"0.1667em"}}]},"” means multiplication, as described in § 2 ‘Notation’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5","href":"#fn5"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["“ZEC/TAZ” refers to the native currency of Zcash on a given network, i.e. ZEC on Mainnet and TAZ on Testnet."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖷"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]}]}]},", as defined in § 5.3 ‘Constants’ ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6","href":"#fn6"}]},", is ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mn","children":["2"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["100"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]}]}," zatoshi."]},{"tag":"p","children":["“Block Subsidy” means the algorithmic issuance of ZEC/TAZ on block creation, as defined by consensus and divided among the miner and any Funding Streams."]},{"tag":"p","children":["“Issuance” means the mechanism by which ZEC/TAZ becomes available for circulation."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes to remove 60% of transaction fees from circulation, while the remaining 40% is directed as before. The intent of this removal is that the funds will be automatically and algorithmically reissued through future block subsidies, rather than being permanently destroyed or held as a discretionary reserve."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["ZIP 233 (“Network Sustainability Mechanism: Removing Funds From Circulation” ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7","href":"#fn7"}]},") describes a method by which ZEC can be removed from circulation to support network sustainability."]},{"tag":"p","children":["By introducing a requirement that a certain proportion of transaction fees be removed from circulation, we aim to contribute to the long-term sustainability of the network as described below:"]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Benefits to the Network"],"id":"benefitstothenetwork"},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Network Sustainability"]},": This mechanism involves temporarily reducing the supply of ZEC, similar to asset burning in Ethereum’s EIP-1559 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8","href":"#fn8"}]},", but with long-term sustainability benefits. Unlike a permanent burn, the removed funds are intended to be reissued through future block subsidies."]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Incentivizing Transaction Inclusion"]},": By maintaining a 40% share of transaction fees for miners, we continue incentivizing miners to prioritize including transactions in their blocks. This helps ensure the continued efficient processing of transactions and supports a robust and responsive network."]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Aligning Interests:"]}," Removing transaction fees from circulation aligns the interests of miners with the long-term health of the network, incentivizing them to prioritize security and efficiency. As miners focus on maintaining a robust network, overall adoption and usage can increase, leading to higher transaction volumes in the long run. This structure discourages short-term profit-seeking behaviors, as miners benefit more from a stable and thriving ecosystem than from engaging in malicious activities that could undermine the network’s reputation and security."]},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Future-Proofing the Network"]},": Removing a portion of transaction fees from circulation is a forward-looking approach that prepares the Zcash network for long-term sustainability. By returning these funds to circulation through future block subsidies, the network maintains a viable security budget beyond the original issuance schedule."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Privacy Implications"],"id":"privacyimplications"},{"tag":"p","children":["The amount removed from circulation and the miner’s fee entitlement are calculated from already-public transaction fees. These calculations disclose no additional transaction information."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Requirements"],"id":"requirements"},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["For each block, 60% (rounded down) of the total fees are to be removed from circulation."]},{"tag":"li","children":["The rule does not require any transaction format change."]},{"tag":"li","children":["No restrictions are placed on the destination of the remaining proportion of fees."]},{"tag":"li","children":["Any fractions are rounded in favor of the miner."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Changes to ZIP 237"],"id":"changestozip237"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes to register the following mechanism for removal from circulation in the list defined in ZIP 237 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9","href":"#fn9"}]},":"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["Mechanism"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Source"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["Transaction fees"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖢"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖻"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["("],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗀"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":[")"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Consensus Rule Changes"],"id":"consensusrulechanges"},{"tag":"p","children":["For the block at height ",{"tag"